+<!doctype html>
+<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow"><meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer"><meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; connect-src 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'"><title>One tort. Two weeks. | Marketing Apes Campaign Sprint</title><meta name="description" content="A focused two-week mass-tort campaign sprint: three intake experiences, Facebook creative, reviewed routing and clear reporting. $7,500: $2,500 build and management plus $5,000 media."><link rel="canonical" href="https://marketingapes.com/campaign-sprint/"><link rel="stylesheet" href="./sprint.css"><script src="./sprint.js" defer></script></head>
+<body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="shell top"><a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="Marketing Apes home">MARKETING APES<span>CAMPAIGN SPRINT / MASS TORT</span></a><a class="nav-cta" href="#pilot">Talk to Kyle <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></header>
+<main id="main"><section class="hero shell"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> FOR MASS-TORT FIRMS</p><h1>One tort.<br>Two weeks.<br><em>A focused campaign sprint.</em></h1><p class="lede">Give your next campaign a focused test, with a clear path from ad to intake. We build the ads, three intake experiences and a reporting plan around <strong>your firm’s criteria.</strong></p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="#pilot">Request a pilot <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="#demo">Explore the demo ↓</a></div><p class="hero-note">Two-week sprint · $7,500 total · launch only after your approval</p></div>
+<div class="hero-panel"><div class="panel-head"><span class="mini-label">YOUR CAMPAIGN, CONNECTED</span><span class="tag">ILLUSTRATIVE</span></div><div class="campaign-identity"><span class="icon-mark" aria-hidden="true">↗</span><div><strong>One campaign brief</strong><span>Your tort · your geography · your intake team</span></div></div><div class="path-line" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="mini-doors"><a href="./demo/form.html"><span>01</span><strong>Form</strong><small>Keep it direct ↗</small></a><a href="./demo/quiz.html"><span>02</span><strong>Quiz</strong><small>Guide each step ↗</small></a><a href="./demo/sofia.html"><span>03</span><strong>Sofia</strong><small>Voice walkthrough ↗</small></a></div><div class="review-gate"><span aria-hidden="true">◎</span><div><strong>Firm-approved routing</strong><small>Criteria, destination and consent reviewed before launch</small></div></div><div class="panel-bottom"><span class="signal" aria-hidden="true"></span> Perspective <span>See the journey, not just the click</span></div><p class="panel-disclaimer">Demo architecture. No live lead, call, transfer or result is shown.</p></div></section>
+<div class="shell flow" aria-label="Demonstrated campaign journey"><span>Draft ad</span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b><span>Page</span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b><span>Fictional intake</span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b><span>Simulated handoff</span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b><span>Perspective demo</span></div><section class="promise"><div class="shell promise-inner"><p>A focused test.<br><strong>With a defined finish line.</strong></p><p>Can the message bring the right inquiries to your intake team—and can we see what happens next? That is what the sprint is designed to evaluate. Results depend on the campaign, market and follow-through.</p></div></section>
+<section class="shell section" id="how"><div class="section-top"><p class="eyebrow">01 / THE PLAN</p><h2>You know the case.<br>We build the path.</h2></div><div class="steps"><article><span class="step-num">1</span><h3>You define the fit</h3><p>Supply one tort, written acceptance and exclusion criteria, geography, intake destination, coverage hours and approved disclosures.</p></article><article><span class="step-num">2</span><h3>We build the campaign</h3><p>One coordinated brief drives form, quiz and Sofia experience drafts, plus three creative concepts for a Facebook-first pilot.</p></article><article><span class="step-num">3</span><h3>Your team reviews</h3><p>Approve copy, consent, routing, assets and media scope. We verify intake and reporting before any enabled experience receives paid traffic.</p></article><article><span class="step-num">4</span><h3>Run, review, decide</h3><p>During the approved two-week media window, review delivery, intake quality and available firm outcomes. Leave with findings and a proposed next test.</p></article></div></section>
+<section class="demo-section" id="demo"><div class="shell section"><div class="section-top"><p class="eyebrow">02 / TRY THE EXPERIENCE</p><h2>Three entry points.<br>One review standard.</h2><p>These fictional examples use the existing Best Tort Lawyers campaign kit. They demonstrate the experience—not your firm’s approved criteria or a working provider integration.</p></div><p><a class="text-link" href="./demo/ads.html">See the three draft ad concepts →</a></p><div class="demo-grid"><article class="demo-card"><span class="door-index">A / DIRECT</span><div class="demo-art form-art" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><b>Continue →</b></div><h3>The standard form</h3><p>A familiar route for people who want to provide the basics at their own pace.</p><a href="./demo/form.html">Try the form preview ↗</a></article><article class="demo-card"><span class="door-index">B / GUIDED</span><div class="demo-art quiz-art" aria-hidden="true"><small>ONE QUESTION AT A TIME</small><b>What happens next?</b><i>Clear choices <span>↗</span></i></div><h3>The guided quiz</h3><p>Structured questions, space for uncertainty and a clear human-review boundary.</p><a href="./demo/quiz.html">Try the quiz preview ↗</a></article><article class="demo-card"><span class="door-index">C / CONVERSATIONAL</span><div class="demo-art voice-art" aria-hidden="true"><div class="wave"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><b>“How can I help today?”</b><small>SOFIA / AI INTAKE WALKTHROUGH</small></div><h3>The Sofia experience</h3><p>See a call-assisted journey. Actual voice, identity checks and transfer behavior require separate setup and verification.</p><a href="./demo/sofia.html">Open Sofia walkthrough ↗</a></article></div><p class="demo-notice"><strong>DEMONSTRATION ONLY.</strong> Use fictional information. Demo forms do not send leads; Sofia does not place or connect calls. No microphone, tracking or external intake connection is enabled.</p></div></section>
+<section class="shell section" id="perspective"><div class="section-top"><p class="eyebrow">03 / PERSPECTIVE</p><h2>Know what happened<br>after the inquiry.</h2><p>In the proposed connected workflow, your authorized team follows source, screening, handoff and firm feedback together. Unknown stays unknown. A transfer attempt is never labeled a signed case.</p></div><div class="journey"><div class="journey-head"><div><strong>Lead journey / DEMO-001</strong><span>FICTIONAL EXAMPLE · NOT LIVE DATA OR PERFORMANCE</span></div><span class="tag">SYNTHETIC</span></div><ol class="timeline"><li><span class="time">STEP 01</span><div><strong>Source & inquiry</strong><p>Facebook → quiz · synthetic submission receipt</p></div><span class="state">Demo received</span></li><li><span class="time">STEP 02</span><div><strong>Screening</strong><p>Example answers awaiting the firm’s review</p></div><span class="state neutral">Needs review</span></li><li><span class="time">STEP 03</span><div><strong>Sofia & handoff</strong><p>No call placed; no destination connected</p></div><span class="state neutral">Not connected</span></li><li><span class="time">STEP 04</span><div><strong>Firm outcome</strong><p>Acceptance, signed case and revenue require firm confirmation</p></div><span class="state neutral">Unknown</span></li></ol><div class="recordings"><div><strong>Sofia recording</strong><span>Unavailable · no demo call exists</span></div><div><strong>Transfer recording</strong><span>Unavailable · provider linkage not verified</span></div></div><p class="journey-foot">No real lead data or recordings. Live reporting and protected recording access depend on approved integrations, consent, verified lineage and authorized firm access.</p></div></section>
+<section class="offer-section" id="offer"><div class="shell offer-layout"><div><p class="eyebrow">04 / THE OFFER</p><h2>A two-week sprint.<br>A defined budget.</h2><p class="offer-intro">One tort. One receiving firm. One approved geography. A focused Facebook-first pilot—not a promise that every channel or integration is already live.</p><ul class="inclusions"><li>Campaign brief, three intake experience drafts and three creative concepts</li><li>Campaign setup, management and a Perspective reporting plan</li><li>Human review of routing, launch scope and the next experiment</li></ul><p class="terms">Final scope and terms are confirmed before invoicing. The two-week media window starts after approvals and technical readiness, not when you click this page. Unverified doors remain off. No lead volume, cost per case, case acceptance or outcome is guaranteed.</p></div><div class="price-card"><span class="mini-label">ONE INVOICE / TWO CLEAR PARTS</span><p class="price">$7,500<span>total pilot budget</span></p><dl><div><dt>Build & management</dt><dd>$2,500</dd></div><div><dt>Media allocation</dt><dd>$5,000</dd></div></dl><p>Media is separate from the service fee within the same invoice. It is not a fee or a second invoice. No payment is collected here.</p><a class="button" href="#pilot">Discuss your pilot ↗</a><small>No automatic launch. No automatic renewal; any continuation requires agreement.</small></div></div></section>
+<section class="shell section contact" id="pilot"><div class="founder"><img src="/assets/vegas/kyle-headshot-480.webp" width="120" height="150" loading="lazy" alt="Kyle Gosselin, founder of Marketing Apes"><span>YOUR CONTACT<br><strong>Kyle Gosselin</strong><br>Marketing Apes</span></div><h2>Which tort should<br>we build around?</h2><p>Send Kyle your firm’s name, tort, target states and intake contact. We’ll confirm fit, scope and what your intake team needs before asking you to commit. Please do not email claimant details or medical records.</p><a class="button" href="mailto:kyleg@marketingapes.com?subject=Mass-tort%20campaign%20sprint%20pilot&amp;body=Firm%20name%3A%0ATort%3A%0ATarget%20states%3A%0AIntake%20contact%3A">Email Kyle about a pilot ↗</a><p class="email-note">Opens your email app. You choose when to send.<br><a href="mailto:kyleg@marketingapes.com">kyleg@marketingapes.com</a></p></section>
+<section class="shell faq"><h2>A few things to know.</h2><details><summary>Is this a live campaign?</summary><p>This page demonstrates the proposed offer. The previews and reporting example are isolated demonstrations. Your campaign is scoped, reviewed and verified before launch.</p></details><details><summary>Will all three experiences run immediately?</summary><p>No. We stage all three, then enable only the experiences that pass approval and technical checks. A verified form can lead the pilot while voice integration remains in review.</p></details><details><summary>Who decides which inquiries your firm accepts?</summary><p>Your firm supplies and approves the criteria. Automated screening is not a legal determination. Human intake review and firm-confirmed outcomes remain separate from marketing signals.</p></details><details><summary>What happens after two weeks?</summary><p>We review the available evidence, reporting gaps and intake feedback together. Any continuation, new channel or additional spend requires a separately agreed scope.</p></details></section></main><footer class="shell footer"><a class="wordmark" href="/">MARKETING APES</a><p>Campaign services for law firms. Best Tort Lawyers is not a law firm. No legal advice, representation or case results are offered by this demonstration.</p><a href="#main">Back to top ↑</a></footer></body></html>
